From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP missing holder is a gap, not a crash

checkNeighbour still threw Missing chunkholder when the neighbour was
unloaded but not an exact cut key (halo / mid-reap). Treat any null
holder as already-at-status and reuse the center in the neighbour cache.
CraftWorld.getChunkAt must not NPE when getChunk(load) returns null.
Carve stays on. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/ChunkTaskScheduler.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/ChunkTaskScheduler.java
@@ -773,11 +773,11 @@
         final StaticCache2D<GenerationChunkHolder> neighbours = StaticCache2D
                 .create(chunkX, chunkZ, neighbourReadRadius, (final int nx, final int nz) -> {
                     NewChunkHolder holder = nx == chunkX && nz == chunkZ ? chunkHolder : this.chunkHolderManager.getChunkHolder(nx, nz);
-                    if (holder == null
-                            && io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.isCutChunk(this.world, nx, nz)) {
-                        // Legal empty-buffer cut: no holder in the hole. Reuse the center so FULL
-                        // load on the kept side does not NPE / Missing chunkholder.
+                    if (holder == null) {
+                        // YaP: corridor unload can drop a neighbour that is not in the exact-key
+                        // cut set (halo / race). Reuse the center so FULL on the kept side proceeds.
                         holder = chunkHolder;
                     }
                     if (holder == null) {
                         throw new IllegalStateException("Missing chunkholder when required");
@@ -804,12 +804,9 @@
         final NewChunkHolder chunkHolder = this.chunkHolderManager.getChunkHolder(chunkX, chunkZ);
 
         if (chunkHolder == null) {
-            if (io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.isCutChunk(this.world, chunkX, chunkZ)) {
-                // Corridor unload dropped the holder. Do not schedule gen into the hole;
-                // treat the gap as already at the required status so the kept side can FULL-load.
-                return false;
-            }
-            throw new IllegalStateException("Missing chunkholder when required");
+            // YaP: no holder means nothing to generate (cut, halo, or mid-unload). Do not throw;
+            // treat as already at the required status so the kept side can FULL-load.
+            return false;
         }
 
         final ChunkStatus holderStatus = chunkHolder.getCurrentGenStatus();
--- a/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftWorld.java
+++ b/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftWorld.java
@@ -373,7 +373,12 @@
         ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.TickThread.ensureTickThread(this.getHandle(), x, z, "Async chunk retrieval"); // Folia - region threading
         warnUnsafeChunk("getting a faraway chunk", x, z); // Paper
         net.minecraft.world.level.chunk.LevelChunk chunk = (net.minecraft.world.level.chunk.LevelChunk) this.world.getChunk(x, z, ChunkStatus.FULL, true);
+        // YaP: a registered corridor hole returns null from getChunk(load) — do not NPE CraftChunk.
+        if (chunk == null) {
+            return new CraftChunk(this.getHandle(), x, z);
+        }
         return new CraftChunk(chunk);
     }
 
     @NotNull
